<h1>Samantha &quot;Sam&quot; Nugent</h1>
<p>39th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.samanthanugent39.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (samanthanugent39.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Filed nominating petitions for reelection on Oct. 19, 2026. Her campaign site asks voters to reelect her &quot;for a safer, better 39th ward,&quot; says her priorities have not changed, and lists safety, schools, the environment, infrastructure, and businesses as her priorities, citing resources against crime and capital improvements at neighborhood schools.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>39th Ward alderwoman since 2019 and the Council&#39;s president pro tempore since 2023; attorney who previously worked for the Illinois Attorney General and the Cook County Department of Homeland Security and Emergency Management.</p>
